1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:01,660
Nico has put up the stake.

2
00:00:02,555 --> 00:00:03,607
One seat is empty.

3
00:00:04,575 --> 00:00:08,010
Fill it with the wrong person, and everyone could go to jail.

4
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:13,636
This is OMERTÀ, a multiplayer mafia strategy RPG in your browser.

5
00:00:15,352 --> 00:00:17,652
Nico starts with a name and a little cash.

6
00:00:18,558 --> 00:00:19,853
He takes a small job.

7
00:00:20,731 --> 00:00:21,684
Nerve goes down.

8
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:23,998
Cash and respect go up.

9
00:00:24,892 --> 00:00:25,450
Now what?

10
00:00:26,345 --> 00:00:28,300
Another job could build his bankroll.

11
00:00:29,177 --> 00:00:31,652
Training spends energy to improve his stats.

12
00:00:32,534 --> 00:00:36,680
Banking protects money once it arrives, but the trip leaves it exposed.

13
00:00:37,605 --> 00:00:39,768
Three choices, different risks.

14
00:00:40,632 --> 00:00:42,792
Nico has to choose what matters next.

15
00:00:43,687 --> 00:00:48,645
That is how a place in this city begins: one decision, then its consequence.

16
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:55,162
As he progresses, six Paths open different ways forward.

17
00:00:55,872 --> 00:00:57,084
The Gun brings street combat.

18
00:00:57,812 --> 00:00:59,289
The Ledger, fronts and trade.

19
00:01:00,008 --> 00:01:01,339
The Kitchen, better cooking.

20
00:01:02,049 --> 00:01:03,540
The Wheel, faster convoys.

21
00:01:04,254 --> 00:01:05,753
The Shadow, quicker searches.

22
00:01:06,464 --> 00:01:08,321
The Ring, stronger duels and bouts.

23
00:01:09,017 --> 00:01:10,369
Every advantage costs something.

24
00:01:11,082 --> 00:01:14,216
Nico chooses the Wheel: faster convoys, slower cooking.

25
00:01:14,932 --> 00:01:15,863
Mara chooses the Gun.

26
00:01:16,592 --> 00:01:19,409
Their specialties are different; their preparation still matters.

27
00:01:20,107 --> 00:01:21,971
Nico starts thinking beyond his next payout.

28
00:01:22,776 --> 00:01:24,942
What can he do that makes someone else want him around?

29
00:01:30,383 --> 00:01:31,830
He buys a sack of coffee.

30
00:01:32,734 --> 00:01:35,903
There is the price, the debit, and the cargo in his trunk.

31
00:01:36,791 --> 00:01:38,943
Getting a bargain is only half the decision.

32
00:01:39,861 --> 00:01:40,729
Goods need moving.

33
00:01:41,625 --> 00:01:42,762
Cars need repairs.

34
00:01:43,654 --> 00:01:45,937
Boats open sea runs with risks of their own.

35
00:01:46,831 --> 00:01:49,973
A business has upkeep; a Kitchen batch takes time.

36
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:55,623
Races, boxing, the Den and the Speakeasy give people other reasons to return.

37
00:01:56,528 --> 00:01:59,985
Loans, auctions and fixers create other opportunities.

38
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:02,643
The city rewards paying attention.

39
00:02:05,362 --> 00:02:09,646
Nico forms a Crew, a small circle for mutual aid and chat.

40
00:02:10,652 --> 00:02:12,667
Then comes the Payroll Office job.

41
00:02:13,657 --> 00:02:15,721
This heist needs a wheelman and muscle.

42
00:02:16,687 --> 00:02:19,619
Nico takes the wheelman role and puts up the stake.

43
00:02:20,601 --> 00:02:22,076
The second seat is empty.

44
00:02:23,067 --> 00:02:23,975
Mara joins.

45
00:02:25,008 --> 00:02:26,166
Both names are there.

46
00:02:27,241 --> 00:02:29,100
Preparation improves their odds.

47
00:02:30,085 --> 00:02:33,015
It cannot tell Nico what somebody else will choose.

48
00:02:34,006 --> 00:02:34,719
He commits.

49
00:02:37,255 --> 00:02:38,274
The law was waiting.

50
00:02:39,253 --> 00:02:40,253
Somebody talked.

51
00:02:41,942 --> 00:02:43,446
Both players go to jail.

52
00:02:45,995 --> 00:02:47,797
The result names no informant.

53
00:02:48,782 --> 00:02:50,998
Nico can read exactly what happened.

54
00:02:51,998 --> 00:02:54,109
He still does not know whom to believe.

55
00:02:58,357 --> 00:02:59,028
Jail ends.

56
00:02:59,911 --> 00:03:01,111
The question remains.

57
00:03:02,017 --> 00:03:03,897
Would you invite the same person again?

58
00:03:04,798 --> 00:03:07,824
Bigger risks can cost more: a character can die.

59
00:03:08,691 --> 00:03:12,440
Your account continues, but an heir keeps only a limited legacy.

60
00:03:13,330 --> 00:03:14,919
Seasons have their own rules.

61
00:03:15,806 --> 00:03:20,984
Eligible gear and vehicles can leave the game, but extracted items stop working inside it.

62
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:25,446
Combat cannot take unrelated assets from your external wallet.

63
00:03:26,433 --> 00:03:27,664
What do you keep in play?

64
00:03:28,563 --> 00:03:30,035
What are you prepared to lose?

65
00:03:32,346 --> 00:03:36,305
Elsewhere in the city, discoveries can be kept private or shared with permission.

66
00:03:37,107 --> 00:03:39,914
Two investigators may need evidence they found independently.

67
00:03:40,704 --> 00:03:42,704
Copying the same clue is not another witness.

68
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:48,634
Objects tell stories too: salvage becomes material, and an eligible recipe makes an item

69
00:03:48,634 --> 00:03:49,840
with a traceable history.

70
00:03:50,654 --> 00:03:57,084
Beyond Nico's small Crew, Families pursue larger ambitions: treasury, territory, rivalries and wars.

71
00:03:57,874 --> 00:04:00,297
Shared operations need contributions and approval.

72
00:04:01,091 --> 00:04:02,357
Convoys can be ambushed.

73
00:04:03,155 --> 00:04:05,581
Commission seats give votes on specific city rules.

74
00:04:06,363 --> 00:04:10,065
Events and the Director's authored situations change the opportunities around you.

75
00:04:12,337 --> 00:04:13,955
Not every rival is at a keyboard.

76
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:16,213
A player can operate an agent.

77
00:04:17,025 --> 00:04:19,594
Here it reads its available actions and takes a street job.

78
00:04:20,382 --> 00:04:22,695
Nerve falls; cash and respect change.

79
00:04:23,476 --> 00:04:25,424
The next decision starts from that new state.

80
00:04:26,295 --> 00:04:28,597
Permissions and resources still limit what it can do.

81
00:04:29,375 --> 00:04:31,175
The city's NPCs are separate.

82
00:04:31,984 --> 00:04:35,971
Whether you bring friends or build an agent, the choices still have consequences.

83
00:04:40,337 --> 00:04:42,551
Nico needs equipment, access and people.

84
00:04:43,342 --> 00:04:46,121
Money helps, but the balances have different jobs.

85
00:04:46,926 --> 00:04:48,515
Game cash pays for city life.

86
00:04:49,315 --> 00:04:54,330
In-game OMR buys selected gear and services; some privileges require holding or staking it.

87
00:04:55,192 --> 00:04:56,920
Most OMR spends recycle it.

88
00:04:57,797 --> 00:05:00,132
Wallet OMR is separate, onchain.

89
00:05:00,937 --> 00:05:03,298
The funded Window spends OMR for game cash.

90
00:05:04,089 --> 00:05:05,461
That conversion goes one way.

91
00:05:06,253 --> 00:05:08,586
Game rewards are not automatic wallet payouts.

92
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:13,058
Trading fees fund developer, community, asset and liquidity budgets.

93
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:16,561
Inventory bonds release existing OMR over time.

94
00:05:17,362 --> 00:05:20,454
Liquidity rewards need eligible positions and funded campaigns.

95
00:05:21,253 --> 00:05:24,032
Some realized arbitrage profit can support reserves.

96
00:05:24,878 --> 00:05:29,249
Families compete for designated trading-fee rights; they do not take the pool's principal.

97
00:05:30,033 --> 00:05:34,349
Real-world assets include Stock Tokens: exposure to assets outside the game.

98
00:05:35,152 --> 00:05:39,280
Commission choices, acquisition, custody and eligibility govern the process.

99
00:05:40,068 --> 00:05:42,548
Holding OMR does not promise everyone a payout.

100
00:05:43,446 --> 00:05:45,585
These systems shape what players can organize.

101
00:05:46,375 --> 00:05:48,256
They cannot decide whom Nico should trust.

102
00:05:51,796 --> 00:05:53,274
The next job comes round.

103
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:54,968
Another stake.

104
00:05:55,845 --> 00:05:56,927
Another empty seat.

105
00:05:57,822 --> 00:06:04,062
Nico has learned how to earn, how to specialize, and how much another person's decision can cost him.

106
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:07,437
The next invitation is a choice he has to make.

107
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:09,391
You can buy equipment.

108
00:06:10,281 --> 00:06:11,482
You cannot buy trust.

109
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:13,257
Choose your path.

110
00:06:14,176 --> 00:06:15,115
Find your people.

111
00:06:15,996 --> 00:06:16,756
Make your name.

112
00:06:17,646 --> 00:06:18,275
OMERTÀ.

113
00:06:19,159 --> 00:06:19,974
Who will you bring?

114
00:06:20,882 --> 00:06:23,019
Start playing at omerta.fun.
